  "solution": {
    "text": "$A^2=\\left(\\begin{array}{cc}1 & 1+i \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right), A^3=\\left(\\begin{array}{cc}1 & i \\\\ 0 & -i\\end{array}\\right), A^4=I$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n&\\therefore A^{2018}=A^{2016} \\times A^2=A^2=\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}\n1 & 1+i \\\\\n0 & -1\n\\end{array}\\right) \\\\\n&\\therefore a+d=1+(-1)=0\n\\end{aligned}$",
